**Table of Contents**

**1. Overview & Platform Decision**

The \[PLATFORM NAME\] mobile app is a first-class product --- not a
companion app or a stripped-down version of the web platform. For field
workers, it is the primary interface. This document specifies the full
mobile app requirements, screens, offline capabilities, native
integrations, and technical implementation decisions.

**1.1 Platform Decision**

> **Decision:**
>
> React Native --- iOS and Android from a single codebase. Rationale:
> shares business logic and component patterns with the React web app,
> significantly reduces development time, has the largest talent pool of
> all cross-platform options, and delivers sufficient performance for
> all required use cases (no 3D graphics or high-frequency animation).

  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Option**   **Pros**                 **Cons**              **Decision**
  ------------ ------------------------ --------------------- --------------
  React Native Code sharing with web,   Slightly below native ✓ SELECTED
               large talent pool, Expo  performance for       
               toolchain, mature        complex animations    
               ecosystem, OTA updates                         

  Flutter      Excellent performance    Dart language         Rejected
               and UI consistency,      (separate skill),     
               growing ecosystem        less code sharing     
                                        with React web        

  Native       Best performance and     Two full codebases,   Rejected ---
  (Swift +     platform integration     2× engineering cost,  not viable for
  Kotlin)                               2× maintenance        v1.0 budget

  Ionic /      Fastest initial dev for  Worst performance,    Rejected ---
  Capacitor    web devs                 webview-based, poor   field use
                                        offline support       requires real
                                                              performance
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------

