**2. Offline-First Architecture**

> **Core Requirement:**
>
> The app MUST work with zero connectivity. Construction sites
> frequently have no reliable cell service. A foreman cannot be unable
> to submit a daily report or clock out their crew because of bad
> signal. Every critical field flow must work offline.

**2.1 Offline Data Strategy**

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Data           **Offline Behavior**  **Storage        **Sync Direction**
  Category**                             Method**         
  ---------------- --------------------- ---------------- -------------------
  Active project   Cached at last sync   SQLite           Read --- server →
  list             --- available offline (WatermelonDB)   device

  Project schedule Full task list cached SQLite           Read + write queue
  (tasks)          --- can mark complete                  
                   offline                                

  Crew list        Employee names and    SQLite           Read only
                   IDs cached                             

  Plan PDFs        Manually              File system ---  Read only --- large
                   pre-downloaded or     React Native FS  files
                   auto-downloaded on                     
                   project open                           

  Daily reports    Created and queued    SQLite write     Write --- device →
                   offline --- uploaded  queue            server
                   on reconnect                           

  Time entries     Clock in/out recorded SQLite write     Write --- device →
                   locally with device   queue            server
                   timestamp --- synced                   
                   on reconnect                           

  Task completions Marked complete       SQLite write     Write --- device →
                   locally --- synced on queue            server
                   reconnect                              

  Photos           Captured and stored   File system +    Write --- device →
                   locally --- uploaded  SQLite queue     server
                   in background when                     
                   connected                              

  Notifications    Not available offline Not cached       N/A
                   --- require                            
                   connectivity                           
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

**2.2 Offline Queue & Sync Engine**

The sync engine is the most technically complex component of the mobile
app. It must handle:

1.  Queue management --- all offline writes are added to a SQLite queue
    table with: action_type, payload JSON, created_at, retry_count,
    status

2.  Background sync --- when connectivity is detected, the queue
    processor runs automatically. It does not require the user to
    manually trigger sync.

3.  Ordered processing --- queue items are processed in created_at order
    to maintain correct sequence (e.g. clock-in before clock-out)

4.  Retry logic --- failed uploads retry up to 5 times with exponential
    backoff

5.  Conflict detection --- server returns a conflict flag if the record
    was modified server-side since last sync. App surfaces a conflict
    banner to the user.

6.  Progress indicator --- sync status shown in the app header:
    \'Syncing 3 items\...\' / \'✓ All synced\' / \'⚠ 2 items pending (no
    connection)\'

7.  Merge pull --- after pushing the queue, app pulls any server changes
    since last sync timestamp

**2.3 Local Database Schema**

The app uses WatermelonDB (a high-performance SQLite-based database for
React Native) for all local data. Key tables mirroring the server
schema:

-   projects --- id, name, status, job_type, sync_at

-   schedule_tasks --- id, project_id, name, status, percent_complete,
    planned_start, planned_end, sync_at

-   employees --- id, name, trade, sync_at

-   time_entries --- id, employee_id, project_id, clocked_in_at,
    clocked_out_at, status (pending \| synced \| failed)

-   daily_reports --- id, project_id, report_date, payload JSON, status
    (draft \| pending_sync \| synced)

-   sync_queue --- id, action_type, entity_type, entity_id, payload
    JSON, created_at, retry_count, status

-   plan_cache_index --- plan_revision_id, local_file_path, file_size,
    cached_at

