**4.3 Geofencing Logic**

-   On clock-in attempt, the app reads device GPS (requires location
    permission)

-   Distance calculated between device GPS and project
    site_address.lat/lng

-   If distance \< 500 feet: green confirmation --- \'You are on site
    ✓\'

-   If distance 500--2000 feet: yellow warning --- \'You appear to be
    near the site. Continue?\'

-   If distance \> 2000 feet: orange warning --- \'You are not at the
    job site. Clock in anyway?\' --- PM is notified

-   If GPS unavailable: allows clock-in with a flag --- PM sees \'(no
    GPS)\' on the time entry

-   Foreman crew clock-in: uses foreman\'s GPS for the entire crew ---
    not each worker\'s device

