**10.2 Release Strategy**

-   Beta: TestFlight (iOS) and Google Play Internal Testing track ---
    30-day beta before public launch

-   Beta users: design partners (first 10 customers), internal team,
    advisory board members

-   Staged rollout: v1.0 launches to 25% of users for 48 hours before
    full rollout --- monitors crash rate

-   OTA updates: JS bundle updates ship via Expo EAS Update for bug
    fixes --- no App Store review required

-   Native updates: any change to native modules (camera, permissions,
    etc.) requires full App Store submission

-   Version policy: minimum supported version maintained for 12 months
    after release --- force-upgrade after that

**10.3 Accessibility Requirements**

-   WCAG 2.1 AA compliance target --- not optional

-   VoiceOver (iOS) and TalkBack (Android) support for all interactive
    elements --- aria labels required

-   Dynamic text size support --- app scales with system font size
    preferences

-   Color contrast: all text meets 4.5:1 minimum contrast ratio ---
    status indicators do not rely on color alone (icons + text labels
    required)

-   Touch targets: minimum 44×44pt on all interactive elements --- no
    exceptions

**11. Internationalization --- Mobile Implementation**

The mobile app is the most critical surface for language support ---
field workers use mobile exclusively, and they are the workers most
likely to have Spanish (or another language) as their primary language.
Every field-facing screen must be fully bilingual at v1.0 launch.

**11.1 react-i18next Mobile Setup**

> // i18n.ts --- root configuration
>
> import i18n from \'i18next\';
>
> import { initReactI18next } from \'react-i18next\';
>
> import \* as Localization from \'expo-localization\';
>
> import enCommon from \'./locales/en/common.json\';
>
> import esCommon from \'./locales/es/common.json\';
>
> // \... other namespaces loaded lazily
>
> const deviceLocale = Localization.locale.split(\'-\')\[0\]; // \'es\',
> \'en\', etc.
>
> const userLocale = await getStoredUserLocale(); // from Keychain /
> SQLite
>
> const resolvedLocale = userLocale \|\| deviceLocale \|\| \'en\';

**11.2 Voice Dictation --- Multilingual Support**

Voice dictation on daily reports and notes must work in Spanish. Both
iOS and Android native speech recognition support Spanish --- no
third-party service required.

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Platform**   **Implementation**           **Spanish   **Notes**
                                              Support**   
  -------------- ---------------------------- ----------- ---------------------------------
  iOS            SFSpeechRecognizer(locale:   Full ---    Locale passed at recognizer
                 Locale(identifier:           es-US,      initialization --- changes with
                 userLocale))                 es-MX,      user\'s language preference
                                              es-ES all   
                                              supported   

  Android        SpeechRecognizer with        Full ---    Pass language extra:
                 languageModel + language     es-US,      RecognizerIntent.EXTRA_LANGUAGE =
                 extras                       es-MX       \'es-US\'
                                              supported   

  Offline        Device on-device speech      ES offline  Prompt user to download Spanish
  fallback       model (iOS: downloaded       model       speech model if not present on
                 model, Android: offline      available   first-time ES selection
                 model)                       on both     
                                              platforms   
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

> // React Native --- language-aware speech recognition
>
> Voice.start(userLocale === \'es\' ? \'es-US\' : \'en-US\');

**11.3 Language Selection UI --- Mobile**

-   First-run experience: if device locale is Spanish, app opens in
    Spanish --- no prompt needed

-   If device locale is not a supported language, app defaults to
    English with a banner: \'Change language in Profile settings\'

-   Profile \> Language: dropdown of supported languages --- changing
    takes effect immediately, all screens re-render in new locale

-   Language change does NOT require re-login --- JWT claims updated via
    a silent /users/me/language PUT call

-   Language selection persisted in WatermelonDB locally --- survives
    offline, survives app restarts

**11.4 OTA Translation Updates**

-   Translation JSON files are bundled with the app but can be updated
    via Expo EAS Update OTA --- fixing translation errors does not
    require an App Store submission

-   On app launch, the sync engine checks for translation updates
    alongside data sync

-   New language additions (e.g. adding PT-BR in v1.1) require a full
    App Store submission --- OTA only for corrections to existing
    translation files

**11.5 String Length & UI Accommodation**

-   All mobile UI components tested with Spanish strings --- ES strings
    are 20-30% longer than EN equivalents

-   Clock-in button: \'Clock In\' (8 chars) → \'Fichar Entrada\' (14
    chars) --- button must accommodate

-   Tab labels shortened if needed for ES: \'Field\' → \'Campo\',
    \'Time\' → \'Tiempo\', \'Docs\' → \'Docs\' (same)

-   Critical safety text (inspection FAILED, weather delay) must never
    truncate --- these messages must be read in full
